      "lyrics": "[Intro]\n[Verse 1]\nI didn't need a fence and I didn't need a hand\nI didn't need the water or the acres of the land\nI sat inside the office with the ledger and the ink\nCreating up a fortune faster than a man can blink\nOne stroke of the pen and a hundred head appear\nGrazing on the paper in the middle of the year\nThey never bawled for mother and they never ate the hay\nBut they satisfied the market at the ending of the day.\n[Pre-Chorus]\nNo blood, no bone, no heavy breathing sound.\nJust a ghost herd walking on the imaginary ground.\n[Chorus]\nPaper Cattle.\nTwo hundred thousand ghosts.\nFeasting on the greed of the unaware hosts\nThey don't leave a track in the muddy winter clay\nBut they're worth a heavy fortune when the gambling debts come due\nYeah the phantom on the spreadsheet is the only thing that's true.\nPaper Cattle.\n[Verse 2]\nThe Chicago board was flashing red and asking for the cash\nI was betting on the future, heading for a crash\nSo I invented me an asset that could cover up the hole\nSold a lie to Tyson just to save a sinner's soul\nThey counted up the inventory sitting in the file\nNever looked inside the feedlot for a country mile\nIt\u2019s amazing what a suit and tie will swallow with a smile\nWhen the profit is the only thing that makes it worth the while.\n[Bridge]\nYou can't slaughter a memory.\nYou can't butcher a dream.\nIt\u2019s the perfect crime inside the perfect scheme.\nUntil the music stops.\n(And the feed bunk is empty.)\n[Chorus]\nPaper Cattle.\nTwo hundred thousand ghosts.\nFeasting on the greed of the unaware hosts\nThey don't leave a track in the muddy winter clay\nBut they're worth a heavy fortune when the gambling debts come due\nYeah the phantom on the spreadsheet is the only thing that's true.\nPaper Cattle.\n[Outro]\nAssets: Two hundred million.\nInventory: Zero."
